4.0 (2026.11.27) - fork, id io.github.zebieksterc.netspeedwidget (installs next to the original):

New in the panel
Optional line with the network name, router latency and Wi-Fi signal (as a filled bar, or as text with a thin bar)
Optional line per data limit: used / limit, percentage, thin bar; a warning triangle when the limit is reached
Optional frame; with a data limit it changes gradually from green through yellow and orange to red
Optional small graph behind the numbers, Wi-Fi signal bar and percentage, dimming while not connected, a small mark while idle
0 or 1 decimal places, digits of equal width; the font size setting also scales the extra lines
Mouse: middle click copies the IP address (IPv4, else IPv6), the wheel switches between bits and bytes
Tooltip: totals, today, limits, signal, network name, router latency, data source, version

New: details popup on click
Current speeds and a graph of the last 60 readings
All connections: peak, session, today, this month; Copy all; Reset (session, today, month, limits, history, everything)
One box per interface: network name, router latency, signal, speed, totals, its data limit, IPv4 and IPv6 addresses (a click copies)
History of the last 12 months
Internet check on request: external IP address and latency to an internet host
One size for the whole popup, set in percent (80 - 200 %)
With "Launch application on click" the details open from the right-click menu

New: counters, limits, notifications
Usage counters for this session, today and this month, optionally per interface; the month can start on any day (1 - 28)
Traffic from the time the widget was not running (Plasma restart, crash, before login) is added at the next start
Up to 8 data limits, each for all connections or one interface, with its own start day and an "already used" start value
Notifications, kept in Plasma's notification history: connection lost and restored, Wi-Fi signal weak, data limit at 80 % and reached, IP address copied
Router latency measured at a chosen interval

Settings
Five tabs: General, Appearance, Connection, Data limits, Advanced; every page scrolls
Options explain themselves on hover; an option without effect in the current combination is dimmed, most with a warning triangle that gives the reason

Changed from 3.1
Speeds come from Plasma's system-monitor sensors: no process is started per update, and VPN/bridge/container traffic is not counted twice
"/proc/net/dev" is only read for selected interfaces, while the details are open, or when the sensors give no data
Launch application on click without the private quicklaunch module (uses kstart or gtk-launch)
Kilobit label is now "kb/s"
Removed files the fork does not use: CMakeLists.txt, release.sh, run.sh, netspeed-widget.png, package/contents/ui/Launcher.qml (README and screenshot of the original are kept as docs/README_upstream.md and docs/README_upstream.png)

Fixes of 3.1
Speeds in bits were shown 2.4 % too high
Negative speeds after an interface was recreated
Old speed stayed on screen when reading failed
Selecting interfaces did not enable the Apply button
Error when choosing an application in the settings
Values just below the next unit were printed as "1000.0" / "1024.0"

Scripts and tests
install.sh (no root; restores the previous version if the installation fails; can install any tagged version), uninstall.sh, check.sh (health check; --try runs the widget in a window of its own)
tests/helpers.test.js (430 tests of the calculations) and tests/harness/ (runs the QML without Plasma)
docs/GUIDE.md: a guide with pictures for first-time users
GitHub Actions workflow: tests, builds the .plasmoid file, publishes a release for a version tag
The notification entry is part of the package; the widget puts it in place itself when it is missing (for installs from a .plasmoid file)

